description:
Design a 24-hour counter that increments an 8-bit output periodically with each rising edge of the clock signal, resetting to zero after reaching 23 (represented as 8'b00100011). The counter supports a synchronous reset and generates a carry-out signal (`count_carry`) whenever it wraps around from 23 back to 0. The upper nibble of the output tracks the tens place of the hour count, incrementing when the lower nibble exceeds 9 and resetting to 0, thus representing a valid 24-hour format.
module top_module(input clk,
					 input reset,
					 output reg[7:0] two_four,
					 output reg count_carry
					 );

code:
module top_module(input clk,
					 input reset,
					 output reg[7:0] two_four,
					 output reg count_carry
					 );always@(posedge clk)begin
	if(!reset||two_four >= 8'b00100011) begin
		two_four <= 8'b00000000;
		count_carry <= 1;
	end
	else if (two_four[3:0] >= 4'b1001)begin
		two_four[7:4] <= two_four[7:4] + 1;
		two_four[3:0] <= 4'b0000;
		count_carry <= 0;
	end
	else begin
		two_four <= two_four + 1;
		count_carry <= 0;
	end
end


endmodule

