description:
Design a Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) generator that produces a PWM signal based on an 8-bit input duty cycle. The module increments a counter on each rising edge of the clock signal, and sets the output high when the counter value is less than the specified duty cycle, effectively controlling the width of the output pulse. The counter resets after reaching a maximum value of 255, enabling periodic modulation of the output signal with a variable duty cycle specified by the duty_cycle input, thus allowing for control over the average power delivered to a load.
module top_module(
    input clk_i,
    input [7:0] duty_cycle,
    output reg pwm_o = 1'b0
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input clk_i,
    input [7:0] duty_cycle,
    output reg pwm_o = 1'b0
    );reg [7:0] pwm_cnt = 0;

	always @(posedge clk_i) begin
		if (pwm_cnt < duty_cycle) begin
			pwm_o <= 1'b1;
		end else begin 
			pwm_o <= 1'b0;
		end
		pwm_cnt <= pwm_cnt + 1;
		if (pwm_cnt == 8'b11111111) begin
			pwm_cnt <= 8'b00000000;
		end
	end

endmodule

