description:
Design a synchronous 4-bit binary counter with asynchronous reset functionality. The counter increments its value on the rising edge of the clock signal (clk) and resets to zero when the reset signal is asserted. It utilizes a series of registers to store intermediate values, effectively creating a delayed feedback loop that introduces additional clock cycles to update the output (Q). This design enables robust counting while maintaining synchrony with the clock for reliable operation in digital circuits.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [3:0] Q
);

