description:
Design a 4-bit Johnson counter that generates a specific sequence of binary numbers. The counter takes a clock and reset signal as inputs; upon reset, it initializes the output to zero. On each rising edge of the clock, it updates its internal state by shifting the bits to the right while setting the most significant bit (MSB) to the complement of the least significant bit (LSB). The current state of the counter is provided as a 4-bit output.
module top_module(
    input clk,reset,
    output [3:0] dout
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,reset,
    output [3:0] dout
    );reg [3:0]temp;
    integer i;

    always@(posedge clk) begin
        if(reset)
            temp<=4'b0000;
        else begin
            temp[3]<=~temp[0];
            for(i=0;i<3;i=i+1) begin
                temp[i]<=temp[i+1];
             end
         end
    end

    assign dout=temp;

endmodule

